WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Further south on the Nile, Meroe was a major centre of Kush.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.600
In the third century BCE, royal burials here used steep-sided pyramids above underground tombs.

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.000
The city and its royal cemeteries formed distinct parts of this landscape.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.950
In north-eastern Africa, Aksum’s great stone stelae were carved in the third and fourth centuries CE.

5
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:20.000
Some turned a single block of stone into the image of a many-storeyed building.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.300
Far to the south, Great Zimbabwe grew into a major trading city.

7
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.600
Its fourteenth-century Great Enclosure shows the skill of its stone builders.

8
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:32.000
The enclosure and conical tower form part of the site’s later architectural ensemble.
